# Fixed-epoch round trip, deliberately NOT a bare `date +%s`: the runner
# executes the subject and the oracle sequentially, so two live clock reads
# straddle a second boundary whenever the runs cross one, and the case then
# reports OUT_DIFF for two correct answers (observed in run 40943010494,
# after PASS in the three preceding baseline runs on the same host clock).
# `-d @1234567890 +%s` keeps the +%s formatting coverage with an
# input-determined answer.
cmd: date
args: -d @1234567890 +%s
timeout: 10
source: github.com/unixwin/WinuxCmd
tags: corpus-expansion round-4
